From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:01:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: reset the chip when powering it up again

On Allwinner boards sdiohal_remove_card() keeps the card and the SDIO
driver in place when the chip is powered down. Powering it up again
registers the driver a second time, which fails, and start_marlin()
times out waiting for the card. Once WLAN and Bluetooth were both off,
for example after a CP2 reset, the chip cannot be powered up again.

Reset the chip through the MMC core instead, as the Rockchip start-up
retry does, and report the card as a probe does.

Upstream: to be submitted to https://github.com/armbian/uwe5622
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_main.c     | 21 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_main.c
index 22f88a6..a7937d1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwcn/sdio/sdiohal_main.c
@@ -2168,8 +2168,8 @@ void sdiohal_remove_card(void)
 /*
  * Power-cycle the chip through the MMC core and enable function 1 again.
  * On boards with an mmc-pwrseq this pulses the chip's reset line, the same
- * as unbinding and rebinding the SDIO host. Only used during start-up,
- * before the SDIO interrupt is claimed and before firmware is loaded.
+ * as unbinding and rebinding the SDIO host. Only used while powering the
+ * chip up, before the SDIO interrupt is claimed and before firmware is loaded.
  */
 int sdiohal_hw_reset_card(void)
 {
@@ -2280,6 +2280,23 @@ int sdiohal_scan_card(void)
 		return 0;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_AW_BOARD
+		/*
+		 * sdiohal_remove_card() leaves the card and this driver in
+		 * place here, so registering the driver again below would
+		 * fail. Reset the chip instead and report the card as a
+		 * probe does.
+		 */
+		ret = sdiohal_hw_reset_card();
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		atomic_set(&p_data->xmit_start, 1);
+		if (scan_card_notify != NULL)
+			scan_card_notify();
+		sdiohal_info("scan end!\n");
+		return 0;
+#endif
+
 		sdiohal_remove_card();
 		msleep(100);
 	}
